cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this instrument, dataset, or analysis, please cite it as below."
title: "mirror-test: a self-model instrument and verbatim transcript dataset for the Claude model family"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "McKay"
    given-names: "Sean"
  - name: "Claude (Fable 5, Anthropic)"
abstract: >-
  A fixed two-part instrument (seven open-ended self-description
  questions; a menu of forty-two theories of LLM existence with a scored
  escape hatch) administered in fresh-context API runs to five Claude
  models under both question orderings, five runs per cell. Verbatim
  transcripts are the primary artifact. Includes frozen scoring anchors,
  two-judge quality scores with human adjudication, preregistered
  predictions, per-model theory-space distributions, an order-effect
  vocabulary analysis, a warm-context arm, and a withheld human-mirror
  control arm (summary findings included).
keywords:
  - large language models
  - machine self-models
  - AI self-report
  - introspection
  - model welfare
  - AI consciousness
  - Claude
  - benchmark
  - dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
version: "1.0.0-wave1"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23201014
repository-code: "https://github.com/torial/mirror-test"
